# {{displayName}}

This application was generated by `scaffold new`. It starts with a {{one.words}} collection and default list and record screens. Replace the generated fields, access rules and screens with those the work at your site needs.

## Run the application

From the project root, open the browser host:

```sh
bun run dev:web
```

The host prints a one-use launch link. `bun run dev` opens a desktop window instead. The starter selects this application in `app.config.json` and stores its local workspace in `.workspace/` by default.

## Change the application

- `contracts/{{one.kebab}}.ts` declares the initial record and its generated reads and writes.
- `handlers/{{one.kebab}}.ts` supplies its handlers; `policy.ts` decides who may call them.
- `ui/{{one.kebab}}.tsx` binds the default screens. `manifest.ts`, `application.ts` and `screens.tsx` compose the browser-safe declarations, server and screens.
- `test/{{one.kebab}}.test.ts` covers the initial behavior. Extend it as you add rules and fields.

Keep the `// scaffold:<list>` markers if you want `bun run scaffold add` to insert collections, capabilities, targets, agents, assignment kinds or features. Generated parts are starting points and need the application's domain behavior. The [getting-started guide](../../../docs/getting-started.md) walks through a change.

## Access and integrations

Only workspace members pass the policy's caller gate. Editors run commands and viewers read; list handlers scope rows before filtering, counting and paging. Configure members and policy for the people doing the work.

The application composes the site, network, audit and compliance host plugins. An added target gives its integration principal no role and limits it to that target's operations. Its generated connector is an in-memory fake; implement and configure a real connector before treating another system's decision as known. The [systems-of-record guide](../../../docs/systems-of-record.md) explains delivery and completion.

## Tests

From the project root:

```sh
bun test showcase/examples/{{app.kebab}}
bunx playwright test showcase/examples/{{app.kebab}}
```

The conformance test reads a list through the instance, HTTP, CLI and MCP; the UI-binding test checks declared screen bindings. The browser test creates, opens and edits {{one.a}} with the default screens. Update the tests as the application changes, and report a real provider, device or system-of-record run separately.
